I fixed the one claim the checker flagged and started the judge re-check. Nothing is needed from you.

## Done
- **Missing verdict fixed.** The checker that compares the campaign's state file with the results table found one claim with nothing behind it. The 10-page document run on seed 42 (job 191378) was listed as closed, but no verdict was on record. I re-read its result file before recording one:
  - the job ended cleanly in 50 minutes;
  - all 1,500 questions are present and the judge scored every answer;
  - the number of compressed slots per question matches the earlier input audit.
- **Judge re-check launched** (job 191517). Our length results so far use one judge prompt. A result only counts once a second prompt agrees: same sign, or within 2 points. I wrote a small launcher, `scripts/longdoc/rejudge.sbatch`. It re-scores copies of the 8 files behind the 10-page and 20-page results with the older yes/no prompt. The original files are not touched.

## Running now
- **Long-document test set build** (CPU job, healthy):
  - 1,407 usable questions on 387 PDFs; 650 of them have their evidence in the text.
  - That is fewer than the 1,500 planned, because of the cap of 6 questions per PDF.
  - 21,843 pages are rendered, and the page-image set (4,221 rows) was being saved.
  - The text, mixed and short-fact sets are still to build.
  - A check that no input gets cut short runs automatically after the build.
- **Text with 40 passages:** the uncompressed run is going. The compressed run was bumped by a higher-priority job and is back in the queue, expected to start around 13:15 tomorrow.
- **Judge re-check:** queued, expected to start around 16:00 tomorrow.

## Next
- When the cut check finishes: small 300-row trial runs on the new long-document sets. These measure time and memory per run.
- Then I will price the full set of model runs. I expect it to exceed the GPU-hours left (about 37). If so, you will get one question with the measured cost.
- If the 40-passage compressed run is still waiting after 03:34, the campaign rules already allow me to move it to the wider queue.

This session cost about $1.73.
